<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi Hollandi Bank H1 1997 net profit soars.</title>
<headline>Saudi Hollandi Bank H1 1997 net profit soars.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			    (million Saudi riyals)</p>
<p> Net profit		 102.5  vs	 76.1</p>
<p> Operating income	  94.0  vs	 67.0</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds  1,304.0  vs    1,165.0</p>
<p> Assets		  17,497.0  vs   15,688.0</p>
<p>Full Name: Saudi Hollandi Bank.</p>
<p>Note - Traded on the Saudi stock market, the Riyadh-based bank is 40 percent owned by the Dutch ABN-AMRO Bank. The rest is held by Saudi investors. -- Bahrain newsroom 973-524424</p>
</text>
